{
  "$comment": "F4 signatures, fixed before any count was taken. One entry per row of ARCHITECTURE.md section 10, in table order. A module (one source file) is a COPY of an item when every predicate in its `all` holds. `role: copy` items count toward `copies`; `role: lib` items only report `libModules` (a consumer using an off-the-shelf equivalent is demand evidence, not a re-implementation). Predicates over one parsed module: import{from,names?} (static, dynamic, require), decl{re} (declared function, class or variable name, any depth; type aliases and interfaces implement nothing and are not decls), call{re} (callee text, `new X` included), ident{re} (any identifier token, property names too), jsxAttr{re}, path{re} (repo-relative path, any file type), dep{re} (package.json dependency name). `any` = at least one of `of`. Test, spec, e2e, d.ts, generated and vendored files are not scanned.",
  "optimistic": {
    "$comment": "state-persistence-forms.md section 9 S4: hand-rolled optimistic updates outside basalt-ui.",
